<section class="usecases" aria-labelledby="usecases-title">
<div class="uc-top">
<h2 id="usecases-title">Use cases for the sites you run</h2>
<p class="uc-lead">One connected system for facilities, assets, and the teams on site.</p>
<div class="uc-nav">
<button class="uc-prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous stories">←</button>
<button class="uc-next" type="button" aria-label="Next stories">→</button>
</div>
</div>
<div class="uc-row">
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Real Estate</h3><p>A property team was running three towers from inboxes and a shared sheet. Requests, vendor visits, and the asset list never sat on the same building.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/real-estate">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Manufacturing</h3><p>Maintenance at the plant was split between the floor and the office. The people beside the line could not see the status the planner had already updated.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/manufacturing">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Healthcare</h3><p>Inspections for clinical rooms and the plant rooms were tracked apart. A check that failed in the morning was hard to find by the afternoon round.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/healthcare">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Corporate</h3><p>Desk bookings, visitors, and workplace requests lived in separate tools. Reception and the workplace team were looking at two different days.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/corporate">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Hospitality</h3><p>Guest requests and the engineering list were kept apart. A room marked ready in one place was still waiting on a repair in the other.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/hospitality">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
<article class="uc-card"><h3>Retail</h3><p>Store faults went into a group chat, and vendor visits sat on a head-office sheet. A repeat fault never showed the last visit.</p><a class="uc-more" href="/stories/retail">Read more <i aria-hidden="true"></i></a></article>
</div>
</section>
<section class="signup" aria-labelledby="signup-title">
<div class="signup-inner">
<div>
<h2 id="signup-title">Run your whole business on one platform.</h2>
<p class="signup-lead">Start free in minutes. No credit card, no setup fees.</p>
</div>
<form class="signup-card" action="#" onsubmit="return false">
<label for="work-email">Work email</label>
<input id="work-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@company.com" autocomplete="email">
<button class="origin-btn primary" type="submit">Start free</button>
<p class="signup-meta"><span>Free plan · Cancel anytime</span><a href="#">Prefer a demo? Book one →</a></p>
</form>
</div>
</section>
<section class="reviews" aria-labelledby="reviews-aside-title">
<div class="rev-row">
<div class="rev-aside">
<span class="rev-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span>
<h3 id="reviews-aside-title">What our customers are saying</h3>
<div class="rev-nav">
<button class="rev-prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous reviews">←</button>
<span class="rev-track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="rev-fill"></span></span>
<button class="rev-next" type="button" aria-label="Next reviews">→</button>
</div>
</div>
<div class="rev-scroller" tabindex="0" aria-label="Customer reviews">
<article class="rev-card"><p>Work across our sites finally sits in one place. Requests, assets, and vendors are visible to the people who need them, and the team actually uses it.</p><div class="rev-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5">★★★★★</div><div class="rev-who"><span class="rev-ph" aria-hidden="true">K</span><div><strong>Karan</strong><span>1 week ago</span></div></div></article>
<article class="rev-card"><p>Facilities and maintenance hand over cleanly now. We stopped chasing status through spreadsheets and long email threads.</p><div class="rev-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5">★★★★★</div><div class="rev-who"><span class="rev-ph g" aria-hidden="true">C</span><div><strong>Catherine</strong><span>10 days ago</span></div></div></article>
<article class="rev-card"><p>We brought the campus onto it without a long rollout. The views match how our teams already run the buildings.</p><div class="rev-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5">★★★★★</div><div class="rev-who"><span class="rev-ph y" aria-hidden="true">P</span><div><strong>Peter</strong><span>2 weeks ago</span></div></div></article>
<article class="rev-card"><p>Inspections, work orders, and vendor visits are on the same record. That removed a meeting we used to need every week.</p><div class="rev-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5">★★★★★</div><div class="rev-who"><span class="rev-ph" aria-hidden="true">A</span><div><strong>Aisha</strong><span>3 weeks ago</span></div></div></article>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<script is:inline>
var r=function(x,y,w,h,q,k){return '<rect x="'+x+'" y="'+y+'" width="'+w+'" height="'+h+'" rx="'+q+'" class="'+k+'"/>'},
c=function(x,y,q,k){return '<circle cx="'+x+'" cy="'+y+'" r="'+q+'" class="'+k+'"/>'},
p=function(d,k,s){return '<path d="'+d+'" class="'+k+'"'+(s?' style="'+s+'"':'')+'/>'},
WIN=r(3,6,36,30,5,'W sD')+p('M3 11a5 5 0 015-5h26a5 5 0 015 5v3H3z','D')+c(8,10,1.1,'W')+c(11.5,10,1.1,'W')+c(15,10,1.1,'W'),
